    "turn_idx": 200,
    "turn_text": "Boom! Fox Across America. With your radio buddy Jimmy Fallon doing the dang thing here in New York City, but... Here's a hot news flash. They're letting me out. You know the Amish let kids go on like a rum springer where they can leave the farm and they can drink and party. Reminds me of the movie Kingpin when the bowler played by Randy Quaid goes out with Woody Harrelson on a bowling binge across the country. They're trying to make some money, take on Bigger and McCracken at the Reno Open. We'll dig this. Fox is letting me off the farm. I am headed out to Royal Oak, Michigan. It is February the 21st. We were at the Royal Oak Theater. We've got a new president. We're doing a new hour of standup. Okay. Because we're back on the road. And if you want to come out, uh, tickets available, Fox across America.com, but I'm telling you now, you are seeing me in my natural habitat. I always issue a disclaimer at the start of a standup show. Cause if you know me from TV and radio, you know that I'm, you know, I'm behaving for the most part. There are some broadcast standards. Wrong. All right. Well, you know, the point is it's a decent upstanding level of commentary that I issue on TV and radio. You are so full of shit. Wow, they're giving me a lot of tough love in the booth. But the point is when I'm doing stand up, I'm in my natural habitat. which means we're saying a lot of things on stage that we can't say on TV or radio, or we'd have a big problem on our hands. I always tell people that I'm kind of like a feral cat. I was a taxi driver in New York City doing stand up here on the circuit, trying to get ahead in life. And I was kind of a feral cat that Fox domesticated. They brought me inside the house, told me how to behave without clawing up the furniture or peeing on stuff for no reason. You know, stand up as my chance to get out of the house and kill a few birds. So if you want to see me in my natural habitat on February the 21st, foxacrossamerica.com, just don't bring any laser pointers to distract the cat is all we ask. All right, back to the show. We got Mark Wayne Mullen coming up. He is on deck. He's a superstar senator from the great state of Oklahoma. He had something to say about the pardons that was so fascinating, but it was Jim Jordan who really summed it up the best. Clip 22. What",
