    "turn_text": "And so it case in point at 2011, I'm training to, uh, to, to, to compete international in Jiu Jitsu. I just won the, uh, uh, an international term when I was frank, I was ranked first in the world in Jiu Jitsu in my, in my division. And, um, I blew my hip out and I went to the doctor and he was like, well, did you have an accident? I was like, no, I was working cattle today. I just couldn't get out of my truck. And he says, no, you had to have an accident. Your hip is trashed. And he says, this may be preexisting. And I was like, well, I don't remember hurt my hip. So what do you do? You call your mom. I picked a phone. I call my mom and she said, Oh, honey, That's the first time I knew that I was born with bad hips. And I was told, the doctors told my parents that I would never compete in sports. And I was like, why didn't you ever tell me that? They said, would it have changed anything? I mean, I went on to the spot professionally. I wrestled collegiate and was doing international sports. And they never told me that because they didn't want it to be an excuse for me.",
